# Conventions

## Context

`app/` is strict TypeScript (`noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is on). Existing modules
(`actions.ts`, `selectors.ts`, `reducer.ts`, `lib/text.ts`) use named exports and
immutable reducer updates. New code must match that style so the custom store
stays predictable and type-safe.

## Rule

- Use **named exports only** — no `export default`
- NEVER use `any` or `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` to silence type errors
- Update state **immutably** in the reducer (spread / `map` / `filter`); never
  mutate objects or arrays in place
- File names: **kebab-case** (e.g. `text-utils.ts`); types/interfaces: PascalCase
- Prefer existing patterns in the file you edit over inventing a new style

## How to verify

1. Grep `app/src` for `export default`, `: any`, `as any`, `@ts-ignore`,
   `@ts-expect-error` — zero matches in new/changed code
2. Reducer tests still pass immutability checks (`cd app && npm test`)
3. New files under `app/src` use kebab-case names
